task: growing-grown-cost
agent: opus5-bench
started: 2026-09-08
branch: feature/growing-grown-cost
worktree: ../okay-wt-grown

why: even when growth is CORRECT, `Growing` at 4 and 16 producers read
  748 and 672 against `adaptive`'s 173 and 112 — 4.3x and 6.0x off the
  very buffer it grew INTO. After the swap the wrapper should cost
  what its inner costs; the layer of call is free (measured 1.02x in
  growing-wrapper-cost).

what: test one specific suspect before anything else. `sample()`
  writes its counter on EVERY push, for ever — the `!grown.get` guard
  is INSIDE the every-64th branch, so the store happens even after the
  buffer has swapped. Growth is one-shot ("one swap, ever"), so every
  one of those stores after the swap is waste; and at 16 producers it
  is sixteen threads storing to one cache line, which is no longer
  false sharing but real contention.

  Fix under test: skip the counter entirely once `grown` is set. That
  trades a per-push volatile read (measured FREE in
  growing-wrapper-cost, variant B: -5 points, nothing) for the removal
  of a contended store.

predict: 4 and 16 producers move from 748/672 toward `adaptive`'s
  173/112; one producer is unchanged, since it never grows and pays
  only the volatile read that measured free.
  DISQUALIFYING: if the numbers do not move, the counter is not the
  cost and the suspect becomes the ADOPTED part 0 — `grow()` passes
  `first = inner`, so part 0 is a full-capacity ring pinned to
  `firstOwner` while every other part is `cap/n`. That is a different
  fix and a different claim, and I will say so rather than keep
  shaving this one.
